invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_flight.c
catches: webpki_encrypted_exts_test
reason: the EncryptedExtensions handler tells the parser the
  ClientHello sent server_name whatever the configuration, so a
  pins-only client without a hostname, whose hello sent none, admits
  an acknowledgement RFC 6066 §3 gives the server no reason to send.
  bin/webpki_encrypted_exts_test's pins-only row objects.

--- old
    rc = hsp_parse_encrypted_exts(raw + 4, raw_len - 4, &t->peer_limit, t->cfg.alpn_protocols,
                                  t->cfg.alpn_count, &t->alpn_selected, t->cfg.hostname_len > 0,
--- new
    rc = hsp_parse_encrypted_exts(raw + 4, raw_len - 4, &t->peer_limit, t->cfg.alpn_protocols,
                                  t->cfg.alpn_count, &t->alpn_selected, 1,
